Description: Fix encryption secrets regenerated on every deploy
 Helm's `default` takes the fallback as its FIRST argument, so
 `default .Values.x (randAlphaNum 32)` evaluates to a fresh random string
 whenever .Values.x is non-empty — inverting the intent. Every `helm upgrade`
 therefore rotated AP_ENCRYPTION_KEY and AP_JWT_SECRET, which invalidates all
 existing sessions and makes previously-encrypted connection credentials
 undecryptable.
Author: Gentian Platform <platform@gentian.org>
Origin: other, https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-apps
Forwarded: not-yet
Bug-Upstream: none filed
Applied-Upstream: no
Last-Update: 2026-08-06
---
diff --git a/templates/secrets.yaml b/templates/secrets.yaml
index 4d75252..288d967 100644
--- a/templates/secrets.yaml
+++ b/templates/secrets.yaml
@@ -19,8 +19,8 @@ metadata:
   {{- end }}
 type: Opaque
 data:
-  connection: {{ default .Values.activepieces.encryption.connection (randAlphaNum 32) | b64enc | quote }}
-  jwt: {{ default .Values.activepieces.encryption.jwt (randAlphaNum 32) | b64enc | quote }}
+  connection: {{ default (randAlphaNum 32) .Values.activepieces.encryption.connection | b64enc | quote }}
+  jwt: {{ default (randAlphaNum 32) .Values.activepieces.encryption.jwt | b64enc | quote }}
 {{- end }}
 ---
